3. What's Already Good
• Clean three-layer split with interfaces (IOperacionServicio, IRepositorioTomi<T>), a SimpleInjector composition root with Verify() (ServiceHost.cs:85), a scoped per-tick configuration clone (ServiceHost.cs:79) and ConfigureAwait(false) consistently in the application layer.
• The orchestration is a readable sequence of guard methods (EsDiaHabilAsync, EstaEnHorarioOperacion) and the shared host gives non-overlapping ticks, a startup/shutdown contract and a cleanup token (TerminacionAsync, ServiceHost.cs:138-178).
• The send loop isolates failures per message (OperacionServicio.cs:332-361: one bad folio does not stop the batch); the MQ connection is closed in a finally (:290-306); the termination marker is written in a finally on every tick (:84-97), so GEN-7 is not present.
• Dynamic SQL is whitelisted and QUOTENAMEd (see §2); all other SQL goes through stored procedures with typed parameters; the stored procedures use XACT_ABORT, explicit transactions, TRY/CATCH with Auditoria.ErrorLog and THROW (SPs 001, 002, 010, 011).
• MQ parameters are validated before connecting (RepositorioTomi.cs:55-62), messages are published with MsgDeliveryMode.Persistent (:323), MapConnectionError turns raw broker exceptions into operator-friendly causes, and no credential value is written to any log.
• Secure XML parsing helper is used for every inbound payload (§2 (b)).
