4.1 AplicacionFCMConector (Tier 0)
MustChange / Rewrite
FCM-FR-6 (Major) - "send, then mark SENT" is not atomic, so a failure between the two steps re-publishes the screening request on the next tick. OperacionServicio.cs:338-345 (loop body of RegistraSolicitudesFCMAsync):
Code block (csharp)
var enviado = await _repositorioTomi.InsertaMensajesFCMAsync(queue, item.Mensaje)...;
if (!enviado) { ...; continue; }
var actualizado = await _repositorioTomi.ActualizaEstatusIntercambioFCMAsync(item.IdEnvio, ConstantesServicio.estatusSENT)...;
if (!actualizado) { Config.EscribirLog(... "Enviado pero no se pudo actualizar estatus" ...); }
Problems: (1) the message is already on the broker when the status update runs; if the update fails the row stays INI (usp_ObtenerOperacionFCM selects estatus='INI', SP 001 line 58) and is published again every tick until the update succeeds - the FCM engine receives the same screening request repeatedly. (2) The if (!actualizado) branch is dead: RepositorioTomi.ActualizaEstatusIntercambioFCMAsync throws InvalidOperationException on failure (RepositorioTomi.cs:180-183) and the per-item catch (:356) logs it, so the caller's documented false contract never happens. (3) On the success path the log line carries the ERROR prefix (:353, see FCM-FR-22). (4) There is no idempotency key (no NMSCorrelationID/message-id property), and the SP update has no row-count check (SP 002 lines 58-60), so a missing id_envio is also "success". Fix: claim first, publish second, finalise third - set INI -> SNDNG (conditional UPDATE ... WHERE estatus='INI', rows-affected checked) before publishing, publish with NMSCorrelationID = IdEnvio.ToString(), then SNDNG -> SENT; add a recovery job/alert for rows stuck in SNDNG. Make the repository return false (or a result object) instead of throwing for an expected failure, and make the caller act on it. Benefit: at-most-once publication per folio, no duplicate screening cases; failures become visible. Suggested JIRA: FCM-6 (Major).
FCM-FR-7 (Major) - broker/DB failures are log-only, and a failed read looks like "no work". OperacionServicio.cs:198-288: ProcesarOperacionesAsync catches everything, writes a log line and returns false; EjecutarProcedimientosAsync (:61-98) only raises an alert (ConstantesClaveAviso.Critico) from its own catch, which can therefore never be reached for a broker outage, a missing queue parameter, a failed RegistraSolicitudesFCMAsync (:220-225) or any of the eight failed queue reads (:271-281). The host discards the returned bool (ServiceHost.cs:125-126). Individually failed folios are also log-only (:342, :356-360) and RegistraSolicitudesFCMAsync returns true even when items failed (:362). Related: RepositorioTomi.RecuperaOperacionesFCMAsync returns resultado.Data without looking at resultado.Exito (RepositorioTomi.cs:140-143). The shared RepositorioMaestro.EjecutarReader catches SqlException/Exception, sets Exito = false and returns an empty list (RepositorioMaestro.cs:202-219), so a database failure is logged by the application as "No existen operaciones FCM para procesar" and the tick returns true (OperacionServicio.cs:322-326). GEN-11. Fix: one tick-result type (Success, NothingToDo, PartialFailure, Failed) returned by every step; alert (deduplicated, see FCM-FR-11) on Failed/repeated PartialFailure; check Exito and throw/return failure in the repository. Benefit: an ActiveMQ or TOMI outage pages someone instead of silently stopping screening. Suggested JIRA: FCM-7 (Major).
Rewrite Recommended
FCM-FR-10 (Major) - required parameters are not validated up front; missing queue names flow on as `null`. OperacionServicio.cs:140,145 use the dictionary indexer (_configuracion.ParametrosSistema[ConstantesServicio.FCMMQHoraInicio]), which throws KeyNotFoundException if the key is absent, while ObtenerValor (:380-387) uses TryGetValue and returns default (= null for the eight queue names, :199-206, and the input queue, :328). A missing queue name therefore becomes ConsultaRespuestaAsync(null, ...) -> false -> a generic "Fallaron las siguientes consultas" log line with no alert (FCM-FR-7). Two different access styles for the same dictionary is the underlying smell. Fix: validate once per tick against the single ConstantesServicio.ParametrosSistema list (the same keys the SP call requests), fail the tick with one alert listing every missing/blank key, and then read with a typed accessor:
Code block (csharp)
var faltantes = Requeridos.Where(k => !p.TryGetValue(k, out var v) || string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(v)).ToList();
if (faltantes.Count > 0) throw new InvalidOperationException("Parametros FCM faltantes: " + string.Join(", ", faltantes));
Benefit: configuration errors fail fast and visibly; no null queue names. Suggested JIRA: FCM-10 (Major).
FCM-FR-11 (Major) - non-business-day / out-of-hours ticks write an ERROR log and a new alert row on every tick; the window predicate is fragile. OperacionServicio.cs:121-132 and :136-164: every tick on a holiday ("Hoy es un día inhábil", :125-129) or outside the window (:158-161) calls RegistrarAlertaAsync(ConstantesClaveAviso.Error, ...). At the 10 s fallback interval that is up to 8,640 alert rows a day for a normal, expected condition (GEN-10). The window test horaActual >= inicio && horaActual <= fin (:155) cannot express an overnight window (inicio > fin never matches), and 00:00-00:00 is used as an "error" sentinel (:148-152), so a legitimately 24x7 configuration (00:00-23:59) is fine but 00:00-00:00 is an error. Fix: log skips at INFO once per state change (keep an in-memory "last skip reason" or reuse the registered-but-unused EstadoHorarioOperacion singleton, see FCM-FR-20) and alert only on state change; support overnight windows (inicio <= fin ? t >= inicio && t <= fin : t >= inicio || t <= fin). Benefit: monitoring noise removed; no silent failure for night windows. Suggested JIRA: FCM-11 (Major).
FCM-FR-16 (Minor) - copy-pasted blocks that should be table-driven. OperacionServicio.cs:198-257 repeats an identical three-statement block eight times (log "Leyendo mensajes del MQ <X>", call ConsultaRespuestaAsync(queue, tipo, nombre), log result): 8 queue-name locals (:199-206), 8 calls (:228-256), a hand-built 8-entry result dictionary (:259-268) and 16 matching constants (ResponseXxx x 8 and ConsultaRespuestaXxx x 8 in ConstantesServicio.cs, plus 8 queue-key constants). The infrastructure project repeats the same shape in 5 near-identical Recupera* methods (see FCM-FR-13) and the application layer 5 near-identical DTOs (FCM-FR-26). Fix:
Code block (csharp)
private static readonly (string Param, string Tipo)[] ColasRespuesta = {
    (ConstantesServicio.FCMMQOutOk, ConstantesServicio.ResponseOK), (ConstantesServicio.FCMMQOutHit, ConstantesServicio.ResponseHIT), /* ... */ };
foreach (var (param, tipo) in ColasRespuesta) resultados[tipo] = await _repositorioTomi.ConsultaRespuestaAsync(ObtenerValor(param), tipo, "ConsultaRespuesta" + tipo);
Benefit: ~60 lines become ~10; adding a ninth queue is one table row. Suggested JIRA: FCM-16 (Minor).
FCM-FR-19 (Minor) - cancellation and shutdown are not handled deliberately. (1) ct is passed only to the control/parameter calls (OperacionServicio.cs:107-112); IRepositorioTomi has no CancellationToken, so an in-progress MQ drain or SQL call cannot be cancelled and a stop waits for it. (2) The catch (Exception ex) at :77 also catches OperationCanceledException, so every service stop mid-tick raises a Critico alert. (3) The finally (:84-97) re-uses the already-cancelled ct for ActualizaTerminacion (:90); on shutdown that call throws immediately and is only logged (:93-96); the host's TerminacionAsync later writes the marker with the cleanup token (ServiceHost.cs:161). Fix: add catch (OperationCanceledException) { throw; } before the generic catch, use CancellationToken.None (bounded timeout) for the terminal marker, and thread ct through IRepositorioTomi. Benefit: clean stop, no spurious critical alerts. Suggested JIRA: FCM-19 (Minor).
FCM-FR-22 (Minor) - misleading log levels and messages. OperacionServicio.cs:353 logs the *successful* SENT update with ConstantesClaveAviso.Error; RepositorioTomi.cs:54 logs "Inicia conexión ... correctamente" before any connection is attempted; RepositorioTomi.cs:800,805 log "Se actualizaron los datos correctamente" regardless of the update result; RepositorioTomi.cs:608 logs "Ocurrio un error al recuperar Calificación" for every ordinary message (a consequence of FCM-FR-2). ConstantesServicio.MensajeErrorConfiguracion is the *info* text "Leyendo archivo de configuración". Fix: correct the levels/texts and log the actual result. Benefit: operators can trust ERROR lines. Suggested JIRA: FCM-22 (Minor).
Nice to Rewrite if Time Permits
FCM-FR-24 (Minor) - `ConstantesServicio` hygiene. ConstantesServicio.cs is a public class of 71 const strings (should be static), 6 are never used (MensajeErrorGeneral, MensajeOnStart, MensajeElapsed, ErrorHora, MensajeDiaInhabil, MensajeFueraDeServicio), 15 trailing lines are commented-out //public const string Mensaje = "";, ParametroWsT24MwPassword is a T24 name used for the MQ user/password parameters, estatusSENT is camelCase, and nuevoEstatus is a constant whose value equals its own name (this is the root of FCM-FR-3). Fix: delete dead constants, rename, make the class static, and group queue constants into the table from FCM-FR-16. Suggested JIRA: FCM-24 (Minor).
**FCM-FR-26 (Minor) - the five Operacion* DTOs are near-duplicates with inconsistent types.** OperacionENTSPEI/ENTSPID/ENTTEF/SERTAX/SPIDTEFFXD (30-38 lines each) repeat nine to eleven fields with private backing fields written as expression-bodied accessors. NF_FOLIO is Decimal in ENTSPEI/ENTSPID but Int64 in the others; MotivoDevolucion is Decimal in ENTSPEI and Int64 in ENTSPID/ENTTEF; OperacionSPIDTEFFXD names its date TF_FECHA_EJECUCION where the others use NF_FECHA_EJECUCION (OperacionSPIDTEFFXD.cs:15,25). Only OperacionSPIDTEFFXD.NF_ESTATUS is ever read (FCM-FR-13). Fix: one DTO (or delete the four unused ones), auto-properties, one type per column. Suggested JIRA: FCM-26 (Minor).
4.2 InfraestructuraFCMConector (Tier 1)
MustChange / Rewrite
FCM-FR-2 (Blocker) - every FCM response except an SPID cut-off writes a blank `estatus` into `tbl_fcm_intercambio` (and the next response inserts a phantom row). RepositorioTomi.cs:604-618 and :740-779:
Code block (csharp)
strCalificacion = await ValidarCancelacionSPID(tipoOperacion, tipoMQ, folioInteger, tabla, campoFolio);   // :604 overwrites the rating looked up at :537
if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(strCalificacion)) Config.EscribirLog("...Ocurrio un error al recuperar Calificación");  // :606-609
var respuesta = await ActualizaDatosOperacion(tipoOperacion, folioInteger, tipoMQ, strCalificacion, mensaje);   // :611
// ValidarCancelacionSPID:  string calificacion = string.Empty;  ... only SPID+HIT+after cut-off sets RECC ...  return calificacion;
For every other response strCalificacion is ""; ActualizaDatosOperacion (:792-811) takes the else branch and calls ActualizaEstatusNotINIFCMAsync(tipoOperacion, folio, tipoMQ, "", mensaje), i.e. usp_ActualizaEstatusNotINIFCM @Estatus = '', which does UPDATE tbl_fcm_intercambio SET estatus = @Estatus ... WHERE nf_folio = @Folio AND estatus IN ('SENT','RECV') (SP 010 lines 88-96). The row is now neither INI, SENT nor RECV, so a second response for the same folio (e.g. HIT followed by OK, or a notification queue) takes the SP's ELSE branch and INSERTs a new row (INSERT INTO tbl_fcm_intercambio (nf_folio, estatus, ...), SP 010 lines 98-104). Every ordinary response also logs a spurious ERROR (FCM-FR-22). (The business table's nf_estatus is written earlier by ProcesarEstatus with the correct value, so only the intercambio table is affected.) Confirmed by reading the C# and the SP; not executed against a database. Fix: let the cancellation rule return an *override* (null = no override) and keep the rating otherwise:
Code block (csharp)
var cancelada = await ValidarCancelacionSPID(...);               // returns RECC or null
var calificacionFinal = cancelada ?? strCalificacion;
Benefit: correct audit trail, no phantom rows, no false error lines. Suggested JIRA: FCM-2 (Blocker).
FCM-FR-3 (Blocker) - the SPID cut-off writes the literal text `nuevoEstatus` into the operation table. RepositorioTomi.cs:757: await UpdateEstatus(tabla, campo, folio, ConstantesServicio.nuevoEstatus); ConstantesServicio.cs: public const string nuevoEstatus = "nuevoEstatus";. For an SPID-family HIT after HORA_SPID_CANCELACION, usp_ActualizaEstatusDinamico sets nf_estatus = 'nuevoEstatus' (11 characters, fits @NuevoEstatus VARCHAR(50), so it succeeds silently) on the payment row, overwriting the RECV status written a few lines earlier. If the following usp_ActualizaEstatusIntercambioCancelFCM call fails, it throws (:213), the outer catch returns "" (:774-778) and the cancel is half-applied. Fix: UpdateEstatus(tabla, campo, folio, ConstantesEstatusPlan.RECC); delete the nuevoEstatus constant; do both writes in one SP/transaction. Benefit: the cancelled payment gets a valid status. Suggested JIRA: FCM-3 (Blocker).
FCM-FR-4 (Blocker) - eight ActiveMQ connections, sessions and consumers are created per tick and never closed. RepositorioTomi.cs:854-858 (LeeMensajesMQAsync, called once per queue by ConsultaRespuestaAsync):
Code block (csharp)
var factory = new ConnectionFactory(servidor);
var connection = factory.CreateConnection(usuario, password);
var session = connection.CreateSession(AcknowledgementMode.AutoAcknowledge);
var consumer = session.CreateConsumer(session.GetQueue(idQueue));
connection.Start();
No Close/Dispose/using exists on any path (normal exit :911, return false :895, catch :913). The connection that CrearConexionApacheNMSActiveMQAsync opened at the start of the tick (:68-72, stored in goMQConnection/goMQSession) is ignored for reads, so each tick opens one used connection plus eight leaked ones - about 2,880 leaked connection objects (each with its own transport thread and socket) per hour at the 10 s fallback interval, until the broker's connection limit or the process's handles/threads run out. Unverified: Apache.NMS finalizer behaviour and the broker's per-client limit. Fix: reuse goMQSession, dispose the consumer, and create the consumer once per queue per tick:
Code block (csharp)
using (var consumer = goMQSession.CreateConsumer(goMQSession.GetQueue(idQueue))) { ... }
Benefit: stable memory/threads/sockets on a service that must run for months. Suggested JIRA: FCM-4 (Blocker).
FCM-FR-5 (Major) - responses are consumed with auto-acknowledge and then processed in a swallow-everything method, so any failure loses the response. RepositorioTomi.cs:857 (AcknowledgementMode.AutoAcknowledge) acknowledges each message as soon as Receive returns (:864). Everything afterwards can fail without a retry: CalificarOperacion wraps its whole body in catch (Exception ex) { Config.EscribirLog(... ex.Message) } (:620-624), so a SQL outage, an unparsable folio (ParseLongRequerido, :548) or an unknown operation type (:542) leave the payment un-updated while the broker already considers the response delivered. Non-text messages (:869-873), invalid XML (:881-886) and messages without folio/tipo_operacion (:902-906) are logged and dropped; an invalid inner payload makes LeeMensajesMQAsync return false mid-queue (:893-897). There is no dead-letter/quarantine and the caller cannot tell a processed message from a lost one. Fix: use AcknowledgementMode.ClientAcknowledge (or a transacted session) and acknowledge/commit only after the database write succeeds; have CalificarOperacion return a result and rethrow on failure; route poison messages to an explicit quarantine queue with a reason and raise an alert. Benefit: no silently stuck screening statuses. Suggested JIRA: FCM-5 (Major).
Rewrite Recommended
FCM-FR-12 (Major) - the status pipeline keeps going after a failed or empty step, so state can be half-applied. CalificarOperacion (RepositorioTomi.cs:490-625): an unparsable/empty folio falls through the guard at :546 with folioInteger = 0 and campoFolio = ""; ProcesarEstatus returns "" on any exception (:671-676) and the caller only logs it (:598-601) before calling ValidarCancelacionSPID and ActualizaDatosOperacion; ProcesarEstatus default branch (:655-658) writes nuevoEstatus = calificacion (an empty string for an unmapped queue type) into usp_ActualizaEstatusDinamico; and the business-table write (UpdateEstatus) and the intercambio write (ActualizaDatosOperacion) are two independent database calls with no shared transaction, so one can succeed while the other fails. Fix: validate -> decide -> persist as one flow with early return on any failed step, and move the two writes into a single stored procedure/transaction. Benefit: the two tables cannot diverge. Suggested JIRA: FCM-12 (Major).
FCM-FR-13 (Minor) - four of five operation look-ups are executed and thrown away; the `INI` path is unreachable. RepositorioTomi.cs:571,575,580,585 await Recupera... for ENT_SPID, ENT_TEF, ENT_SPEI, SER/TAX without assigning the result; only the SPID/TEF/FXD branch is stored (:567) and only valores.FirstOrDefault().NF_ESTATUS is used (GetSubStatus, :683-700). For the other operation families valores is empty, so the fourth character of the current status is lost and the new status is always CON0/HOT0. Whether that is intended is unknown (confirm with the business owner); if it is, the four SP calls and the three DTOs are pure overhead, otherwise the sub-status is a defect. Separately, calificacionMap (:499-509) never yields INI, so case ConstantesEstatusPlan.INI (:651-652), the INI branch of ActualizaDatosOperacion (:797-801), ActualizaEstatusINIFCMAsync (:232-246) and usp_ActualizaEstatusINIFCM are unreachable. Fix: decide and either implement the sub-status for every family (one generic ObtenerEstatusActual(tabla, campoFolio, folio)) or delete the dead calls/DTOs/branch. Suggested JIRA: FCM-13 (Minor).
FCM-FR-14 (Major) - the SPID cut-off rule uses a substring match and a second clock. RepositorioTomi.cs:745-753: DateTime.Now.ToString("HH:mm") is formatted and re-parsed (ParseTimeSpanRequerido) instead of using DateTime.Now.TimeOfDay or the system clock the application layer already uses (_parametrizacion.ObtenerHoraSistema(), OperacionServicio.cs:138); and tipoOperacion.Contains(TipoOperacion.SPID) is a substring test that also matches ENT_SPID (inbound), SPID_Local, SPID_GPH, SPID_H2H and PaP_SPID, so an inbound SPID that gets a HIT after the cut-off is also cancelled. There is no upper bound, so every HIT from the cut-off until midnight is cancelled. If any of that is intended it is undocumented; if not, it cancels payments that should stay. A missing HORA_SPID_CANCELACION throws (ObtenerParametro, :824-831) and the outer catch silently disables the rule. Fix: an explicit HashSet<string> of cancellable operation types, one injected clock, and a required-parameter check (FCM-FR-10). Suggested JIRA: FCM-14 (Major).
FCM-FR-15 (Major) - `RepositorioTomi` is a 922-line god class with business rules in the infrastructure layer and 11 public methods that are not on the interface. It combines MQ connection management (:47-125), publishing (:298-330), consuming/XML parsing (:347-390, :843-912), six SQL operations, five operation look-ups and the whole status state machine (CalificarOperacion, ProcesarEstatus, ValidarCancelacionSPID, ActualizaDatosOperacion, :490-811). IRepositorioTomi exposes only 6 members, so CalificarOperacion, UpdateEstatus, ActualizaEstatusDinamicoAsync, ActualizaEstatusINIFCMAsync, ActualizaEstatusNotINIFCMAsync, ActualizaEstatusIntercambioCancelFCMAsync and the five Recupera* methods can be tested only through a live DB + broker. The generic parameter TSolicitudFCM (:26) and IRepositorioTomi<Tipo> are never used, and the MQ handles are public mutable fields (:29-30). Fix: split into IFcmBroker (connect/publish/consume), IFcmIntercambioRepository (SQL only) and an application-layer RespuestaFcmProcessor holding the maps and rules, so the rules (FCM-FR-2, 3, 12, 14) become unit-testable. Suggested JIRA: FCM-15 (Major).
FCM-FR-17 (Major) - full MQ payloads are written to the log. RepositorioTomi.cs:879 ("Mensaje recibido: {mensaje}", every message) and :617 (mensaje={mensaje} on every success) log the complete response XML, which carries payment/party data (the DTO fields include beneficiary names, amounts, company names). :888 additionally strips every &amp; from the payload before parsing (xmlEntrada.Replace("&amp;", "")), altering data and hiding malformed input. No credential is logged (verified), so GEN-5 is not present for secrets; this is the same class of exposure for personal/financial data. Fix: log queue, folio, operation type, length and a hash; keep the body only in msg_out (by design). Suggested JIRA: FCM-17 (Major).
FCM-FR-18 (Major) - `Int64` folios are sent as `SqlDbType.Int`. RepositorioTomi.cs:403,420,437,454,471 build new SqlParameter("@Folio", SqlDbType.Int) { Value = folio } for an Int64 and the five usp_ObtenerDatos* procedures declare @Folio INT (SPs 004-008), while usp_ActualizaEstatusIntercambioFCM, ...NotINIFCM and ...Dinamico take BIGINT and the repository's other calls use basedatosConexion.CrearParametro. A folio above 2,147,483,647 makes the look-up throw and the exception is swallowed by CalificarOperacion (FCM-FR-5). Fix: SqlDbType.BigInt/@Folio BIGINT (or CrearParametro) everywhere. Suggested JIRA: FCM-18 (Major).
FCM-FR-23 (Minor) - two shared constant files are compiled in as linked source from a path that does not exist in the repository layout. InfraestructuraFCMConector.csproj lines 83-88 include ..\..\..\1. Generales\MUFG_T24 - General\MUFG_T24\Core\Constantes\ConstantesEstatusPlan.cs and ConstantesTablasTombin.cs. Both files already belong to the MUFG_T24 project (MUFG_T24.csproj compiles Core\Constantes\ConstantesEstatusPlan.cs and ...TablasTombin.cs, namespace MUFG_T24.Comunes), so the same types now exist twice (in MUFG_T24.dll and in this assembly) - a compiler CS0436 warning and a drift risk - and the relative path resolves to Mexico\1. Generales\..., which is absent here (the source is under General\MUFGT24_BTMUM_64), so the project only builds on a machine with the original folder layout. Fix: remove the linked Compile items and use the MUFG_T24 copies (part of the GEN-1 fix). Suggested JIRA: FCM-23 (Minor).
